   "source": ["---\n", "## Ejercicio 1: Dunder Methods — El Corazón de Python\n", "\n", "**Concepto:** Python no tiene \"operadores\" como C++. Todo se hace con dunder methods (double underscore). `a + b` llama a `a.__add__(b)`. `len(a)` llama a `a.__len__()`. Al implementar estos métodos, tus objetos \"se sienten\" como nativos de Python.\n", "\n", "**Los más importantes:**\n", "- `__init__`, `__repr__`, `__str__`: Creación y representación\n", "- `__add__`, `__mul__`, `__sub__`: Aritmética\n", "- `__eq__`, `__lt__`, `__hash__`: Comparación y hashing\n", "- `__getitem__`, `__setitem__`, `__len__`: Indexación\n", "- `__enter__`, `__exit__`: Context managers\n", "- `__call__`: Objeto ejecutable\n", "- `__iter__`, `__next__`: Iteradores"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["# Ejemplo: Vector2D con dunder methods completos\n", "import math\n", "\n", "class Vector2D:\n", "    __slots__ = (\"_x\", \"_y\")  # Ahorro de memoria\n", "\n", "    def __init__(self, x, y):\n", "        self._x, self._y = x, y\n", "\n", "    def __repr__(self):\n", "        return f\"Vector2D({self._x}, {self._y})\"\n", "\n", "    def __add__(self, other):\n", "        return Vector2D(self._x + other._x, self._y + other._y)\n", "\n", "    def __abs__(self):\n", "        return math.hypot(self._x, self._y)\n", "\n", "    def __getitem__(self, i):\n", "        return (self._x, self._y)[i]\n", "\n", "v1 = Vector2D(3, 4)\n", "v2 = Vector2D(1, 2)\n", "print(v1 + v2)   # Vector2D(4, 6)\n", "print(abs(v1))   # 5.0\n", "print(v1[0])     # 3"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["# EJERCICIO 1: Implementa una clase Matriz que soporte:\n", "# __init__, __repr__, __add__ (suma), __mul__ (producto), __eq__, __len__, __getitem__\n", "# __getitem__ debe aceptar matriz[fila, col]\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["---\n", "## Ejercicio 2: Descriptors — El Protocolo Oculto de Python\n", "\n", "**Concepto:** Un descriptor es un objeto con `__get__`, `__set__`, o `__delete__`. Cuando accedes a `obj.attr`, Python busca descriptors en la clase. `property`, `classmethod`, `staticmethod` son descriptors.\n", "\n", "**Flujo:** `obj.attr` → `type(obj).__dict__['attr'].__get__(obj, type(obj))`\n", "\n", "**Ejemplo real:** Django Fields, SQLAlchemy Column, Pydantic Field."]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["class Validated:\n", "    def __init__(self, tipo):\n", "        self.tipo = tipo\n", "\n", "    def __set_name__(self, owner, name):\n", "        self.name = name\n", "\n", "    def __get__(self, obj, objtype=None):\n", "        if obj is None: return self\n", "        return obj.__dict__.get(self.name)\n", "\n", "    def __set__(self, obj, value):\n", "        if not isinstance(value, self.tipo):\n", "            raise TypeError(f\"{self.name} debe ser {self.tipo.__name__}\")\n", "        obj.__dict__[self.name] = value\n", "\n", "class Persona:\n", "    nombre = Validated(str)\n", "    edad = Validated(int)\n", "\n", "    def __init__(self, nombre, edad):\n", "        self.nombre = nombre  # Valida automáticamente\n", "        self.edad = edad\n", "\n", "# Persona(\"Ana\", 30)  # OK\n", "# Persona(\"Ana\", \"30\")  # TypeError!"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["# EJERCICIO 2: Crea un descriptor PositiveFloat que:\n", "# a) Valide que el valor sea float positivo\n", "# b) Lance ValueError si no lo es\n", "# c) Funcione como property con getter y setter\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["---\n", "## Ejercicio 3: Patrón Observer — Event-Driven Architecture\n", "\n", "**Concepto:** Observer define una relación 1:N entre objetos. Cuando un objeto cambia (Subject), todos los dependientes (Observers) son notificados automáticamente.\n", "\n", "**Ejemplo real:** Sistemas de eventos en UI (click handlers), patrón pub/sub en microservicios, signals en Django."],
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["from collections import defaultdict\n", "\n", "class EventEmitter:\n", "    def __init__(self):\n", "        self._handlers = defaultdict(list)\n", "\n", "    def on(self, event, callback):\n", "        self._handlers[event].append(callback)\n", "\n", "    def emit(self, event, *args, **kwargs):\n", "        for handler in self._handlers[event]:\n", "            try:\n", "                handler(*args, **kwargs)\n", "            except Exception as e:\n", "                print(f\"Error en handler: {e}\")\n", "\n", "# Uso:\n", "emitter = EventEmitter()\n", "emitter.on(\"datos\", lambda d: print(f\"Recibido: {d}\"))\n", "emitter.emit(\"datos\", {\"sensor\": 42})"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["# EJERCICIO 3: Implementa EventEmitter con:\n", "# a) on(evento, callback) — registrar\n", "# b) emit(evento, *args) — notificar\n", "# c) off(evento, callback) — desregistrar\n", "# d) Manejo de errores para callbacks que fallen\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["---\n", "## Ejercicio 4: Patrón Strategy — Algoritmos Intercambiables\n", "\n", "**Concepto:** Strategy encapsula un algoritmo detrás de una interfaz. El cliente puede cambiar el algoritmo en runtime sin modificar el código que lo usa.\n", "\n", "**Ejemplo real:** Estrategias de caching (LRU, LFU, TTL), métodos de pago, algoritmos de compresión."]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["from typing import Protocol\n", "\n", "class CompressionStrategy(Protocol):\n", "    def compress(self, data: bytes) -> bytes: ...\n", "    def decompress(self, data: bytes) -> bytes: ...\n", "\n", "class ZipCompression:\n", "    def compress(self, data: bytes) -> bytes:\n", "        import zipfile, io\n", "        buf = io.BytesIO()\n", "        with zipfile.ZipFile(buf, 'w') as zf:\n", "            zf.writestr('data', data)\n", "        return buf.getvalue()\n", "\n", "class GzipCompression:\n", "    def compress(self, data: bytes) -> bytes:\n", "        import gzip\n", "        return gzip.compress(data)\n", "\n", "class Compressor:\n", "    def __init__(self, strategy: CompressionStrategy):\n", "        self._strategy = strategy\n", "\n", "    def comprimir(self, data: bytes) -> bytes:\n", "        return self._strategy.compress(data)"]
  },
  {
