   "source": ["---\n", "## Ejercicio 6: Patrón Factory con Registry\n", "\n", "**Concepto:** Factory crea objetos sin especificar la clase exacta. Registry permite registrar y crear plugins dinámicamente.\n", "\n", "**Ejemplo real:** Django form factories, pytest fixtures, plugin systems."]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["class PluginRegistry:\n", "    _plugins: dict[str, type] = {}\n", "\n", "    @classmethod\n", "    def register(cls, nombre):\n", "        def decorator(klass):\n", "            cls._plugins[nombre] = klass\n", "            return klass\n", "        return decorator\n", "\n", "    @classmethod\n    "    def create(cls, nombre, **kwargs):\n", "        return cls._plugins[nombre](**kwargs)\n", "\n", "@PluginRegistry.register(\"busqueda\")\n", "class MotorBusqueda:\n", "    def buscar(self, query): return f\"Resultados para {query}\"\n", "\n", "motor = PluginRegistry.create(\"busqueda\")\n", "print(motor.buscar(\"python\"))"]
  },
